Fillets: the corner where a face cuts the last two walked pieces of a
blend (PerformMoreSurfdata, mitcad#121): the contact on one side has left
its face across an edge of the face at the end while the other runs on to
another edge of it, crossing a face boundary on the way (e.g. a rounding
round a rod where it meets a pipe whose top is flush with the rod's top,
the rod's rounded side and its narrow bevel at the top).

- ChFi3d_Builder::MoreSurfdata: a point of the last but one piece on
  either of the two edges of the face at the end, at either point of the
  last piece, now qualifies. Before, the second point was only compared
  with the edge that happened to be found second among the vertex's
  edges, so the same corner went to PerformMoreSurfdata or, with its
  edges in the other order, to PerformOneCorner, which drops the last
  piece (one of its sides lies on no face) and fails ("Failed to find
  edge").
- PerformMoreSurfdata: where the face cuts the last piece along a curve
  that leaves it through its end section instead of reaching the point on
  arc (the contact reaches the edge to the face at the end there, and the
  piece dips under the face next to it because the faces' normals are
  more than a right angle apart), the piece's surface is extended beyond
  its end (GeomLib::ExtendSurfByLength, as at the end of a stripe cut by a
  face) and cut again; the extended surface replaces the piece's. A
  curve that starts and ends at the point on arc (the face only touches
  the piece there) is not taken for the cut.
- PerformMoreSurfdata: the two pieces meet within their tolerance only
  (the walk restarts a little beyond the previous piece's end): the ends of
  the section and of the cuts are matched to the nearer point, and the
  curves' orientations follow from the nearer pair of ends
  (ChFi3d_ContinuesCurve), where before an end farther than 1e-4 from the
  point made the section run to the other side of the piece and the
  edges' orientations come out inconsistent (an unorientable shell). The
  points' tolerances cover the gap.
- PerformMoreSurfdata: where the section's p-curve on the previous piece
  cannot be projected (it lies on that surface's boundary), it is the
  segment between its ends' parameters, as between two pieces in
  ChFi3d_FilDS. Before, the edge had no p-curve on that face.
- PerformMoreSurfdata: the contact line of the last piece is trimmed at
  the point on arc where the piece runs on beyond it (prolonged for the
  face at the end to cut it); before, the whole line became the edge.
